  {
   "label": "CAPITAL RETURNS:",
   "text": "FY11-25 OCF $14.16B less cash PP&E $5.27B left **$8.89B FCF**. Buybacks **$7.81B (87.9%)**; dividends **$0**. The $1.08B remainder sits before other investing and financing flows; it is not idle cash."
  },
  {
   "label": "NET SHARES:",
   "text": "Split-adjusted shares went from 1,553.7M (FY10) to 1,304.4M (FY25), **down 16.0%**. FY25 alone: 56.8M bought less 2.4M issued = **54.4M fewer (4.0%)**, with buybacks at 167.6% of FCF."
  }
 ],
 "commentary": [
  {
   "headline": "Unit growth hid a traffic problem.",
   "body": "New restaurants added $808.8M of FY25 sales while comps took away $191.3M. Average unit sales slipped from $3.21M to $3.10M, so growth came from more boxes, not busier ones. Mature-store sales are the number to watch as new units open."
  },
  {
   "headline": "Margins wait on traffic.",
   "body": "Q3 2026 transactions +0.8% and check +1.3%, yet restaurant margin fell from 24.5% to 23.3%. Labor leverage needs repeat visits, not price."
  },
  {
   "headline": "New units need time.",
   "body": "257 of 334 FY25 openings had a Chipotlane. Ramp takes up to 36 months; compare cohorts at equal age before crediting the format."
  },
  {
   "headline": "Payback is the real test.",
   "body": "9M26 capex rose to $640.6M from $468.9M. At ~$1.3M net build cost, cohort cash after rent and upkeep must cover the outlay. Rising capex with flat unit sales stretches payback."
  },
  {
   "headline": "Leases change the return math.",
   "body": "Operating lease liabilities were $5.08B at FY25. The 73.5% Base ROIC excludes them; returns must hold once lease capital is counted."
  },
  {
   "headline": "The DCF asks for traffic, not hope.",
   "body": "Base value $41 (8.5% WACC, 3% g) needs FCF/sh to compound ~12% to FY30 with flat margins. At $36.64 the market prices ~9%; mine sits 6.8% below Morningstar."
  }
 ],
